6002:
Track max path corr error\n
\n
\t\n
Check joint definition
7001:
Welding equipment error\n
EPROM checksum error in Welddata Unit\n
detected at power up.\n
\t\n
EPROM in Welddata Unit is faulty.\n
Running with this error gives\n
unpredictable result.\n
Exchange EPROM.
7002:
Welding equipment error\n
Internal RAM read/write error in\n
Welddata Unit detected at power up.\n
\t\n
At least one memory cell in internal\n
microprocessor memory failed in read\n
/write test. Running with this error\n
gives unpredictable result.\n
Replace Welddata Unit.
7003:
Welding equipment error\n
External RAM read/write error in\n
Welddata Unit detected at power up.\n
\t\n
At least one memory cell in external\n
microprocessor memory failed in read\n
/write test. Running with this error\n
gives unpredictable result.\n
Replace Welddata Unit.
7004:
Welding equipment error\n
DC supply voltage for 5 Volt regulator\n
in Welddata Unit has been down.\n
\t\n
Indicates that there is a problem in\n
power supply but the function is\n
probably not affected. Check incoming\n
power supply to Welddata Unit.
7012:
Welding equipment error\n
Welddata Unit CAN-controller for\n
internal bus is in WARNING state.\n
\t\n
Change data several times or reset\n
welding equipment with power switch.\n
If the error do not disappear, check\n
bus connections and/or exchange\n
Welddata Unit.
7013:
Welding equipment error\n
Welddata Unit CAN-controller for\n
external bus is in WARNING state.\n
\t\n
Change data several times or reset\n
welding equipment with power switch.\n
If the error do not disappear, check\n
bus connections and/or exchange\n
Welddata Unit.
7014:
Welding equipment error\n
Welddata Unit CAN-controller for\n
internal bus is in BUS-OFF state.\n
\t\n
Reset welding equipment with power\n
switch. If the error do not disappear,\n
check bus connections and/or exchange\n
Welddata Unit.
7015:
Welding equipment error\n
Welddata Unit has detected that a\n
received internal CAN message was lost\n
(Overwritten by a later message).\n
\t\n
Reset welding equipment with power\n
switch.
7016:
Welding equipment error\n
Welddata Unit has detected that a\n
received external CAN message was lost\n
(Overwritten by a later message).\n
\t\n
Reset welding equipment with power\n
switch.
7017:
Welding equipment error\n
Welddata Unit lost contact with\n
Wirefeed Unit.\n
\t\n
Check connection cable between Welddata\n
Unit and wirefeed control board, check\n
power supply to wirefeed control board.
7018:
Welding equipment error\n
Welddata Unit has lost contact with\n
Olivia Unit.\n
\t\n
Check connection cable between\n
Welddata Unit and Olivia unit, check\n
power supply to Olivia Unit
7019:
Welding equipment error\n
Non-volatile RAM data value failure\n
detected in Welddata Unit at power up.\n
Checksum error.\n
\t\n
Probably caused by low memory backup\n
battery voltage. Welding equipment\n
will be reset to a default state. Data\n
in Welddata Unit will be lost.\n
Possible to run without limitations.
7020:
Welding equipment error\n
Non-volatile RAM data value failure\n
detected in Welddata Unit at power up.\n
Non numeric setting parameter out of\n
range.\n
\t\n
Welding equipment will be reset to a\n
default state. Data in Welddata Unit\n
will be lost. Possible to run without\n
limitations.
7021:
Welding equipment error\n
Invalid combination of non-numeric\n
setting parameters in Welddata Unit\n
detected at power up.\n
\t\n
Welding equipment will be reset to a\n
default state. Data in Welddata Unit\n
will be lost. Reset welding equipment\n
with power switch.
7022:
Welding equipment error\n
CAN-bus (external) transmit buffer\n
overflow in Welddata Unit.\n
\t\n
Welddata Unit are unable to transmit\n
data at the needed rate. Could be\n
caused by unnormal occupation on the\n
bus. Reset welding equipment with\n
power switch.
7023:
Welding equipment error\n
CAN-bus (external) receive buffer\n
overflow in Welddata Unit.\n
\t\n
Welddata Unit are unable to process\n
received messages at the needed rate.\n
Reset welding equipment with power\n
switch.
7024:
Welding equipment error\n
Fragments not in number order when\n
Welddata Unit received a fragmented\n
message.\n
\t\n
The parts of a fragmented message were\n
not received in proper order. A weld\n
data block transmission has been faulty\n
received. Reset welding equipment with\n
power switch.
7025:
Welding equipment error\n
Incompatible format of weld data block.\n
Welddata Unit received data that is\n
stored in another program version with\n
other format version.\n
\t\n
Find data with correct version or enter\n
new data.
7026:
Welding equipment error\n
Program execution error.\n
Watch dog in Welddata Unit program\n
activated.\n
\t\n
Reset welding equipment with\n
power switch.\n

7027:
Welding equipment error\n
Undocumented Welddata Unit error.\n
\t\n
Request additional information from\n
ESAB/ABB.
7028:
Welding equipment error\n
Undocumented Welddata Unit error.\n
\t\n
Request additional information from\n
ESAB/ABB.
7029:
Welding equipment error\n
Undocumented Welddata Unit error.\n
\t\n
Request additional information from\n
ESAB/ABB.
7201:
Welding equipment error\n
EPROM checksum error in Powersource\n
Control Unit.\n
\t\n
EPROM in Powersource Control Unit is\n
faulty. Running with this error gives\n
unpredictable result.\n
Replace EPROM.
7202:
Welding equipment error.\n
Internal RAM read/write error in\n
Powersource Control Unit detected at\n
power up.\n
\t\n
At least one memory cell in internal\n
microprocessor memory failed in read\n
/write test. Running with this error\n
gives unpredictable result.\n
Replace Powersource Control Unit.
7204:
Welding equipment error\n
DC supply voltage to 5 Volt regulator in\n
Powersource Control Unit has been down.\n
\t\n
Indicates that there is a problem in\n
power supply but the function is\n
probably not affected. Check incoming\n
power supply to Powersource Control Unit
7205:
Welding equipment error\n
High DC inverter bus voltage. Hardware\n
will shut down inverter till voltage\n
comes down to normal.\n
\t\n
Might be caused by high mains impedance\n
or transients, possible to restart\n
welding as soon as voltage has dropped\n
below limit.
7206:
Welding equipment error\n
Temperature in power source heatsink too\n
high. Inverter is shut down until\n
temperature switch is closed again.\n
\t\n
Ensure that there is no obstacle that\n
reduces the cooling airflow that passes\n
through the heatsink of the powersource.\n
Wait until temperature switch is closed.
7207:
Welding equipment error\n
High current in inverter circuit. Might\n
be caused by component failure.\n
\t\n
Reset welding equipment with power\n
switch. Check that the power source does\n
not consume unnormal high current\n
without start command. If so: there is\n
a component failure.
7208:
Welding equipment error\n
PCB supply voltage 15VC on Powersource\n
Control Unit to high or to low.\n
\t\n
Replace Powersource Control Unit.
7209:
Welding equipment error\n
PCB supply voltage -15V on Powersource\n
Control Unit to high or to low.\n
\t\n
Replace Powersource Control Unit.
7210:
Welding equipment error\n
PCB supply voltage 15VB on Powersource\n
Control Unit to high or to low.\n
\t\n
Replace Powersource Control Unit.
7211:
Welding equipment error\n
Long term difference between requested\n
and actual weld current value.\n
\t\n
Hardware problem in current servo system\n
(Power source control board or inverter\n
block) or unnormal load conditions\n
(= bad welding).
7212:
Welding equipment error.\n
Internal CAN communication failure CAN\n
circuits in Powersource Control Unit\n
is in WARNING state.\n
\t\n
Change data several times or reset\n
welding equipment with power switch. If\n
the error do not disappear, check bus\n
connections and/or exchange Powersource\n
Control Unit.
7215:
Welding equipment error\n
Powersource Control Unit has detected\n
that a received internal CAN message was\n
lost (overwritten by a later message).\n
\t\n
Reset welding equipment with power\n
switch.
7226:
Welding equipment error\n
Program execution error.\n
Watch dog in Powersource Control Unit\n
program activated.\n
\t\n
Reset welding equipment with\n
power switch.
7227:
Welding equipment error\n
Undocumented Powersource Control Unit\n
error.\n
\t\n
Request additional information from\n
ESAB/ABB.
7228:
Welding equipment error\n
Undocumented Powersource Control Unit\n
error.\n
\t\n
Request additional information from\n
ESAB/ABB.
7229:
Welding equipment error\n
Undocumented Powersource Control Unit\n
error.\n
\t\n
Request additional information from\n
ESAB/ABB.
7301:
Welding equipment error\n
EPROM checksum error in Wirefeed unit\n
detected at power up.\n
\t\n
EPROM in Wirefeed unit is faulty.\n
Running with this error gives\n
unpredictable result.\n
Exchange EPROM.
7302:
Welding equipment error\n
Internal RAM read/write error in\n
Wirefeed Unit detected at power up.\n
\t\n
At least one memory cell in internal\n
microprocessor memory failed in read\n
/write test. Running with this error\n
gives unpredictable result.\n
Replace Wirefeed Unit.
7304:
Welding equipment error\n
DC supply voltage for 5 Volt regulator\n
in Wirefeed Unit has been down.\n
\t\n
Indicates that there is a problem in\n
power supply but the function is\n
probably not affected. Check incoming\n
power supply to Wirefeed Unit.
7308:
Welding equipment error\n
PCB supply voltage 15V on Wirefeed Unit\n
to high or to low.\n
\t\n
Replace Wirefeed Unit.
7309:
Welding equipment error\n
PCB supply voltage 24V on Wirefeed Unit\n
to high or to low.\n
\t\n
Replace Wirefeed Unit.
7311:
Welding equipment error\n
Long term difference between requested\n
and actual wirefeed velocity.\n
\t\n
Hardware problem in wirefeed servo\n
system or voltage drop in 42 V\n
AC supply.
7312:
Welding equipment error\n
Internal CAN communication failure\n
CAN circuits in Wirefeed Unit is in\n
WARNING state.\n
\t\n
Change wirefeed speed several times\n
or reset welding equipment with power\n
switch. If the error do not disappear,\n
check bus connections and/or exchange\n
Wirefeed Unit.
7315:
Welding equipment error\n
Wirefeed Unit has detected that a\n
received internal CAN message was lost\n
(overwritten by a later message).\n
\t\n
Reset welding equipment with power\n
switch.
7326:
Welding equipment error\n
Program execution error.\n
Watch dog in Wirefeed Unit program\n
activated.\n
\t\n
Reset welding equipment with\n
power switch.\n

7327:
Welding equipment error\n
Undocumented Wirefeed Unit error.\n
\t\n
Request additional information from\n
ESAB/ABB.
7328:
Welding equipment error\n
Undocumented Wirefeed Unit error.\n
\t\n
Request additional information from\n
ESAB/ABB.
7329:
Welding equipment error\n
Undocumented Wirefeed Unit error.\n
\t\n
Request additional information from\n
ESAB/ABB.
7500:
Open file error\n
File name unknown\n
\t\n

8000:
Ext CAN com failure\n
Too many requests without response\n
\t\n
Check communication configuration
9000:
Installation error\n
External axes are not allowed in this\n
type of robot configuration\n
\t\n
Remove mechanical units
